AD  - Sardar Patel University, Himachal Pradesh, Mandi, 175001, India
AB  - Early and accurate detection of plant diseases is crucial for improving crop health and minimizing agricultural losses. This paper proposes a novel hybrid deep learning model that integrates Vision Transformers (ViT) for capturing global image dependencies and lightweight Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) for efficient local feature extraction. The model is further enhanced with Grad-CAM, an explainability technique that highlights disease-affected regions, ensuring interpretability and transparency in predictions. Evaluations were conducted on RGB image datasets of apple and mango leaves. The proposed model achieved state-of-the-art accuracy of 98.9% on the apple dataset and 98.5% on the mango dataset, outperforming existing architectures such as AlexNet, ResNet-50, and Efficient-Net. The results validate the effectiveness and scalability of the proposed method for real-world applications in smart farming and precision agriculture. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
