AD  - Zhejiang Institute of Economics and Trade, Zhejiang, Hangzhou, China
AB  - To address the engineering challenges in agricultural disease diagnosis, including scarce data, insufficient model generalization ability, and limited computing power for edge deployment, this study proposes a new intelligent diagnosis paradigm integrating meta-learning and multi-source data fusion, and constructs a cloud-edge collaborative system. The core innovations are as follows: (1) A cross-attention-based multi-source data fusion method (CAM-Fusion) is proposed, enabling the model to maintain an average performance retention rate of 96.6% in cross-domain scenarios, an improvement of more than 8.5 percentage points compared with the baseline; (2) A meta-learning strategy of 'frozen backbone + lightweight adapter' (FBN-LA) is designed, achieving a Top-1 accuracy of 89.4% under the 10 -shot few-shot setting, with a total model parameter size of only 6.02 MB. The system achieves real-time diagnosis of 38 FPS in actual test fields, increasing the efficiency of disease survey by more than 10 times, and reduces potential crop yield loss by 15-20 %. In field tests, the system achieved real-time diagnosis at 38 FPS, boosting disease survey efficiency by more than 10 times, and is estimated to reduce potential crop yield losses by 15-20 %. This study not only validates the effectiveness of the technical route but also, through detailed engineering analysis, provides feasible technical solutions and data support for transitioning from laboratory prototypes to practical field applications.  © 2026 IEEE.
