AB  - The suggested system offers a novel model for the automatic crop health diagnostics and the accuracy application of agrochemicals in the field that exploits the multimodal sensor fusion combined with on-device deep learning. By mixing data from various sources such as visual images, environmental sensors, and spectral data, the system is able to provide a holistic understanding of crop conditions in real-time. At the core of this method is the use of a CNN-based deep learning model implemented directly on edge devices, thus enabling local decision-making without the need for continuous cloud connection. This on-device intelligence not only enables quick detection of crop stress or disease but also allows targeted agrochemical intervention as a result of which the waste and environmental impact are minimized. Multiple sensor modality fusion assures better diagnostic accuracy while the deep learning model is fine-tuned for lightweight deployment, thus allowing the spread of the system in different agricultural environments. The proposed approach is pivotal in promoting sustainable, productive, and smart farming through the implementation of advanced sensor technology and AI-driven processing at the field level. © 2025 IEEE.
