AD  - Academia Sinica, Research Center for Information Technology Innovation, Taipei, Taiwan
AD  - Purdue University, School of Electrical and Computer Engineering, West Lafayette, IN, United States
AB  - We present MoESEC, a Mixture of Experts (MoE) framework that unifies sparse MoE coding with resource-aware wireless optimization, enabling reliable and low-latency semantic communication across heterogeneous edge nodes. Unlike monolithic semantic codecs, MoESEC activates a single specialized expert per input, adapting expert ratio (model capacity) to the computational budget of each device. We further introduce the graphics processing unit (GPU) roofline performance model that couples floating-point performance with memory bandwidth to evaluate end-to-end latency. Building on this, we formulate a system-level optimization problem that jointly allocates expert ratios, subcarriers, and transmission power. An iterative heuristic Double Deep Q-Network (DDQN) optimization framework is proposed to maximize semantic accuracy under per-user Quality of Service (QoS) requirements. When deployed on heterogeneous edge nodes under varying channel conditions, MoESEC achieves significant latency reduction while preserving high semantic accuracy. By aligning semantic sparsity with communication and hardware constraints, MoESEC offers a scalable and robust foundation for real-time edge intelligence. © 2026 IEEE.
