AD  - Isabela State University Cauayan Campus, College of Computing Studies, Information and Communications Technology, Philippines
AB  - The detection of fruit maturity needs to achieve precise accuracy because it serves as the foundation for boosting harvesting productivity and making agricultural intelligence system decisions. The research introduces CalabashSeg+ which functions as a deep learning framework that performs automatic instance segmentation and maturity assessment of Crescentia cujete (calabash) fruit. The research method tests YOLOv8-seg models which include three variations (n s m) and Mask R-CNN through polygon-based image testing that includes three fruit development stages (Immature Mature Overmature) and complex multi-fruit testing situations. The experimental results demonstrate that YOLOv8-seg models achieved high segmentation performance because Mask mAP50 achieves 0.995 and the system maintains class segmentation accuracy above 0.992. YOLOv8n-seg demonstrated the most favorable accuracy-efficiency balance among the evaluated models because it achieves 2.4 ms processing time per image with 3. 2 6 ∼ M parameters outperforming Mask R-CNN in terms of inference speed under the evaluated conditions that needs 54.93 ms per image. The results indicate that lightweight models can achieve accurate maturity detection while maintaining real-time capability. The CalabashSeg+ framework provides an effective solution that enables automated fruit maturity assessment in agricultural settings. © 2026 IEEE.
