AB  - Early identification of tomato leaf diseases is vital for protecting crop health and boosting yield. This study proposes a hybrid model that combines Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) with Transformers to classify tomato leaf diseases with high accuracy. Using a dataset of 20,680 images sourced from Kaggle, the model leverages CNNs for detailed feature extraction and Transformers for capturing global context. This integration allows the system to recognize both local patterns and broader image features effectively. The model achieved impressive results, with an accuracy of 98.76%, precision of 99.10%, recall of 98.95%, and a mean Average Precision (mAP@50) of 98.90%. Compared to traditional CNN-based models, the Transformer-enhanced approach demonstrated notable improvements across all performance metrics. These outcomes highlight the model's effectiveness and reliability in automated disease detection. Its adoption can support timely diagnosis, helping farmers manage crop health proactively and enhance overall agricultural productivity.  © 2025 IEEE.
